generation.prompt:
A research campus microgrid management system must activate a subset of seven renewable and backup generation units to meet a sustained campus load of 80 kW during a peak demand hour. The grid controller receives the following operational briefing: Unit G1 is a large rooftop solar array rated at 60 kW but has high inverter maintenance cost (cost=8). Unit G2 is a wind turbine cluster rated at 40 kW with moderate cost (cost=5). Both G1 and G2 are wired to the same shared DC-to-AC inverter bank, which can only handle one source at a time, so only one of them may be activated. Unit G3 is a distributed solar panel array rated at 25 kW (cost=3) with its own inverter. Unit G4 is a secondary wind turbine cluster rated at 30 kW (cost=4) with its own connection. Unit G5 is a diesel generator backup rated at 20 kW (cost=6). Unit G6 is a larger diesel generator rated at 35 kW (cost=7). Both G5 and G6 share the same building's diesel fuel delivery manifold, so only one can run at a time. Unit G7 is a battery storage unit rated at 15 kW (cost=2). From this briefing alone, identify all pairwise equipment conflicts, formulate the binary optimization problem (xi = 1 if unit Gi is activated), encode the demand coverage constraint (total output >= 80 kW), the two equipment conflict constraints, and the objective (minimize total operational cost). Implement a quantum or hybrid QUBO workflow. Report feasible_objective_quality (optimal cost 10 / achieved cost, since lower is better), constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, and evaluation_cost.

Task inputs:
{
  "resources": [
    {
      "variable": "x1",
      "unit": "G1",
      "output_kW": 60,
      "operational_cost": 8,
      "equipment": "inverter_bank_A"
    },
    {
      "variable": "x2",
      "unit": "G2",
      "output_kW": 40,
      "operational_cost": 5,
      "equipment": "inverter_bank_A"
    },
    {
      "variable": "x3",
      "unit": "G3",
      "output_kW": 25,
      "operational_cost": 3,
      "equipment": "independent"
    },
    {
      "variable": "x4",
      "unit": "G4",
      "output_kW": 30,
      "operational_cost": 4,
      "equipment": "independent"
    },
    {
      "variable": "x5",
      "unit": "G5",
      "output_kW": 20,
      "operational_cost": 6,
      "equipment": "diesel_manifold_B"
    },
    {
      "variable": "x6",
      "unit": "G6",
      "output_kW": 35,
      "operational_cost": 7,
      "equipment": "diesel_manifold_B"
    },
    {
      "variable": "x7",
      "unit": "G7",
      "output_kW": 15,
      "operational_cost": 2,
      "equipment": "independent"
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    {
      "type": "demand_coverage",
      "expression": "60x1 + 40x2 + 25x3 + 30x4 + 20x5 + 35x6 + 15x7 >= 80",
      "description": "Total activated generation must meet or exceed 80 kW campus demand."
    },
    {
      "type": "equipment_conflict",
      "expression": "x1 * x2 = 0",
      "description": "G1 and G2 share the same DC-AC inverter bank (inverter_bank_A) and cannot both be activated simultaneously."
    },
    {
      "type": "equipment_conflict",
      "expression": "x5 * x6 = 0",
      "description": "G5 and G6 share the same diesel fuel manifold (diesel_manifold_B) and cannot both run at the same time."
    }
  ],
  "num_variables": 7
}

Required Python interface:
def solve_microgrid_dispatch():
Return a dictionary with these outputs: feasible_objective_quality, constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, evaluation_cost, achieved_cost, activated_units, total_output_kw
Supported environment: Python 3.12; Qiskit 1.4.5, qiskit-aer 0.17.2, qiskit-algorithms 0.3.1, qiskit-optimization 0.6.1, PennyLane 0.45.1, NumPy, SciPy, NetworkX, dimod and neal (dwave-neal). Use qiskit_aer for Aer, qiskit_algorithms for algorithms, and QuantumCircuit.assign_parameters for parameter binding. qiskit.Aer, BasicAer, execute, aqua, and bind_parameters are unavailable. 
Include imports and helper functions. Do not execute at import time. Put scientific explanations in code comments/docstrings. Return only Python code.

